00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:12.160
Here is how it works when a cheap contract and an expensive one do not earn the same return.

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:17.240
In a paramutual market, the favorite long shot bias is a pattern in returns,

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:19.380
not a slogan about who is clever.

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:25.540
Expected return on an outcome tends to rise as that outcome takes a larger share of the bets.

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:30.900
Long shots on that definition are the side where return has historically been worse.

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:34.800
Favorites are the side where return has historically been better.

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:41.320
A 2010 paper in the American Economic Journal, Microweconomics, treats the pattern as a claim

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:41.920
to test.

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:47.860
It ties both the direction and the size of the bias to one ratio, private information

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:48.680
against noise.

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:52.700
The paper says that ratio should show up in things you can count.

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:54.360
How many people are betting?

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:56.080
How many outcomes are listed?

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:58.780
How much private information is in the market?

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:01.280
How much of the crowd is there for recreation?

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:08.000
Whether a bet can be split into small pieces, whether noise shows up after the event, whether

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:11.020
the outcomes were already unequal before the betting started.

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:15.960
A September 2026 paper hunts for the same pattern on polymarket.

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:21.660
The sample is 588 million trades from 2.48 million accounts.

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:28.360
In the trades as they actually printed, a purchase under $0.10 lost 19.3 on the dollar.

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:33.460
A purchase at $0.90 or higher earned $8,300 of a cent on the dollar.

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:36.860
Change how you group the contracts and the loss flips.

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:42.320
Weight every contract the same and long shots lost $0.6.3 per dollar.

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:48.520
Group related contracts by their parent event first and those long shots gained $0.4.1

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:49.340
per dollar.

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:55.360
The two-sided pattern, cheap contracts losing and expensive ones gaining a little, held

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:56.880
in crypto and in politics.

00:04:56.880 --> 00:05:02.280
statistics. It was absent in sports. The 10th of accounts with the strongest past habit

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:09.080
of buying long shots made 26.6% of the next month's low price purchases. Their returns

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:14.720
looked like everyone else's. They earned less than the rest. The paper's claim is an aggregate

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:20.000
favorite long shot bias on polymarket, and the size of it depends on how the contracts

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:26.040
are grouped. A price near zero or a price near one is not on this evidence a clean reading

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:31.920
of probability. Sports, politics and crypto did not deliver the same return at the same price,

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:37.940
and neither did two ways of grouping one event. Those numbers are a description of past trades.

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:43.020
They are not a reason to take either side of any contract. Before we go,

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:47.860
the next predict summit is still ahead, and a major bank is now on the program.

